1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,353
I grabbed the wrong bag. Same canvas,
same zipper. Mine had been left

2
00:00:05,353 --> 00:00:07,000
under a motel chair.

3
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:12,385
Lucia opened my prize. Toothpaste.
Sandals. Receipts. She laughed until

4
00:00:12,385 --> 00:00:14,000
she found keys.

5
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:19,056
The parking tag matched the car our
buyer had arrived in. We had

6
00:00:19,056 --> 00:00:21,000
accidentally taken his overnight bag.

7
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:27,588
Then my phone buzzed. He had my bag, and
wanted twice the fee to give it

8
00:00:27,588 --> 00:00:28,000
back.

9
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:33,444
Lucia held up his keys. Through the
curtain, his car sat beneath a sign

10
00:00:33,444 --> 00:00:35,000
warning about overnight towing.

11
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:39,667
I sent one photograph. Keys, parking
tag, towing sign. No threats. Just

12
00:00:39,667 --> 00:00:42,000
three things he would recognize
immediately.

13
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:47,056
Five minutes later, my bag appeared
outside our door. We placed his bag

14
00:00:47,056 --> 00:00:49,000
beside it, with everything inside.

15
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:54,833
I checked the cash. Lucia checked my
face. Next time, she said, buy a bag

16
00:00:54,833 --> 00:00:56,000
in another color.
